'''Wall Breaker Seal''' is an earth-type [[Spells|spell]] used for destroying solid materials.

==Description==
Wall Breaker contains a central earth sigil, two column signs to the sides of the earth sigil, and crushing signs at 90-degree angles from the column signs. This spell breaks through objects it is drawn on, reducing the material to dust.

==Usage==
Wall Breaker was first used by [[Richeh]] while she and the other apprentices of [[Qifrey's Atelier]] broke through a wall to escape a [[Dragon|dragon]] in the artificial city created by the [[Illusory Labyrinth]] spell.{{Ref|m|6|12}} It in part helped to inspire the [[Serpent's Bed of Sand]] spell, and was later used by [[Coco]] to help rescue [[Custas]] after he became trapped under a boulder.{{Ref|m|11|17}}

Wall Breaker also served as the inspiration behind [[Integration|Coco's spell for Tartah]], making use of the inversion of the crush signs.{{Ref|m|17|4}}

Tetia often uses this spell as a base for her sand spells, such as in the seal for [[Sand Cage]]{{Ref|m|28|20}} and possibly in her [[Flowers of Sand]] as well.{{Ref|m|24|14}}

==Trivia==
*The Wall Breaker Seal is the spell that has gone through the most revisions, with three in total, though some of these were corrected between the magazine and volume publications.{{Ref|m|6|12}}{{Ref|m|11|17}}{{Ref|m|28|11}}

